id: jf-935b
title: Classify non-OpenAPI Jellyfin CLI surfaces in coverage research
description: "Correct agent-facing Jellyfin API coverage evidence so commands backed by WebSocket, optional legacy plugin routes, and OpenAPI orchestration are not reported as missing REST endpoint mappings; keep exact endpoint coverage and genuine unmatched tools distinct across structured formats."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[10]: agents,api,coverage,jellyfin-10.11.11,openapi,plugins,read-only,research,typescript,websocket
created_at: "2026-08-05T19:15:54.840Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-05T19:58:44.792Z"
assignee: codex-jellyfin-api-20260805
author: codex-jellyfin-api-20260805
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "schema coverage and schema research distinguish direct OpenAPI mappings, local commands, and intentional non-endpoint transports without false unmatched-tool claims; OpenAPI orchestration, WebSocket events, and optional notification plugin routes carry deterministic machine-readable reasons in TOON JSON YAML Markdown table and raw output; Notification read commands honor every advertised output format and unavailable optional routes remain structured and non-mutating; Official 10.11.11 sources and live read-only evidence are documented without server URL, credentials, entity IDs, or raw payloads entering Git or PM; Focused tests, complete release validation, linked PM tests, compiled jf-cli read-only acceptance, privacy checks, and exact-head GitHub checks pass"
definition_of_ready: All-status PM duplicate search completed; latest pm-cli verified; clean main checkout; official latest stable and live server both 10.11.11; owner-only settings valid; no live mutation required.
goal: jf-mqpo
value: Give agents truthful coverage evidence that separates transport architecture from actual API gaps.
impact: Prevents automated roadmaps from chasing false endpoint gaps and makes optional plugin behavior format-safe and diagnosable.
outcome: A deterministic multi-surface coverage model with zero false unmatched tools on the configured 10.11.11 server and documented compatibility boundaries.
why_now: "The current live report says all 429 operations are mapped but simultaneously reports seven unmatched tools, six of which are intentionally not one-to-one REST commands and one of which targets an optional route absent from the official schema."
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: github-review-bots
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11
release: next-manual-release
