comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T19:15:54.840Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260805,"Reviewed the complete 45-item all-status PM inventory, graph health, closed OpenAPI/event/compatibility lineage, latest official Jellyfin sources, and sanitized live schema results before creation; no duplicate plan exists."
  "2026-08-05T19:39:47.208Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260805,"Release validation passes: 981 Bun tests with 183 live skips, 971 portable Vitest tests, release policy, build, package smoke tests, 155-file source LOC gate, secrets and history scans, and changelog check. Explicit compiled live run then passed 183 of 183 tests against 10.11.11 under JELLYFIN_READ_ONLY=1. Trivy is clean; bun audit is clean after safe transitive override refresh. Existing project goals remain honest: coverage is 42.22 statements, 42.30 branches, 52.43 functions, 41.96 lines; jscpd reports 8.14 percent duplicated lines."
  "2026-08-05T19:58:44.792Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260805,"Exact-head bot review disposition: accepted executable full_scope.unmatched_tools_total release assertion and exhaustive coverage-schema fields/reason enums; focused typecheck, lint, 50 tests, and LOC gate pass. Rejected changing pm-changelog importer capability because pm health reports the exporter loaded and the PM capability contract has importers but no exporters capability. Rejected preserving the dated changelog heading on feature branches because docs/RELEASING.md and changelog:pm:check explicitly require Unreleased outside release preparation."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T19:15:54.840Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260805,"Privacy boundary: raw schemas, URLs, credentials, IDs, and live payloads remain owner-only under ~/.jellyfin-cli. PM and Git may retain only public versions, aggregate counts, classifications, commands, and sanitized outcomes."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T19:15:54.840Z",codex-jellyfin-api-20260805,"Coverage of server operations and coverage of CLI transports are different sets: WebSocket, plugin-only, local, and OpenAPI orchestration tools must not be forced into one-operation fuzzy matches."
